# Five warnings from the three strings above the comment, and nothing from the six quiet lines.
# `${name}` and the bare `{name}` are the same mistake in two spellings -- round 2 found the first,
# round 3 found an agent inventing the second and concluding from --check that it works. Each `{`
# is its own site, as deprecation warnings are. Widening the rule to any brace adds two of the
# quiet lines; dropping the scope gate adds `${missing}` as well.
lint 13:11 '${total}' in this string is not interpolation
lint 14:11 '${cfg.host}' in this string is not interpolation
lint 14:11 '${cfg.port}' in this string is not interpolation
lint 15:11 '{cfg.host}' in this string is not interpolation
lint 15:11 '{total}' in this string is not interpolation
